# DESIGN — <capability id>

**Change class:** TRIVIAL | ROUTINE | MATERIAL
**Base revision:** <the full 40-character revision this design was frozen against>
**Frozen:** yes

Written **before** the implementation it governs, and read by
`tools/design_record.py`, which is composed into `capability_open.py`. It
reports; it authorises nothing.

Pick the class honestly, and note that the class is the whole scaling rule:

| Class | What it means | What this file must state |
|---|---|---|
| `TRIVIAL` | reversible, local, promising nothing new | nothing — no record required |
| `ROUTINE` | real work inside a design that already exists | the mechanism, and acceptance + negative oracles |
| `MATERIAL` | a new promise, authority or boundary, or a change to one | all of it |

A `MATERIAL` record with one candidate design is refused, because a single
candidate is a decision nobody made.

## The mechanism

One sentence, in terms of what the machine actually does — not the symptom, not
the file. `skills/core/oracle-discipline.md` is the same rule applied to
oracles, and it is the same rule for the same reason.

