## Authority boundaries

What this may decide, and — more importantly — what it must never decide. A
mechanism that does not say what it must never decide will eventually decide
it. State explicitly that it does not weaken any row of
`policy/hitl-matrix.md`, or state which row it touches and why that is a
governance change (HITL row 7).

## Oracles, frozen before implementation

| ID | Kind | The property it settles | Selector |
|---|---|---|---|
| O1 | ACCEPTANCE |  |  |
| O2 | NEGATIVE |  |  |
| O3 | MUTATION |  |  |

`ACCEPTANCE` — what must hold. `NEGATIVE` — what must be refused.
`MUTATION` — the guard, deliberately broken, demonstrated to fail.
`REHEARSAL` — a sequence, run end to end.

A named oracle that selects no real test is a wish. Fill the selector in as
soon as the test exists, and check it the way the closure matrix already does.
